sentences.text:
Ld. Trial Court has assailed the same on primarily following grounds as under:
(i) That the impugned order is bad in law, perverse, illegal and passed without application of judicial mind;
(ii) That the impugned order passed by Ld. Trial Court is arbitrary and based on conjectures and surmises;
(iii) That Ld. Trial Court failed to appreciate the fact that no person can pass a better title then he himself has and thus, transfer of 163 sq. yards area of property in question in joint ownership amounts to preparation of forged and fabricated documents by the accused persons;
(iv) That Ld. Trial Court failed to appreciate the fact that respondents deliberately prepared wrong recitals in sale deed documents presented before Sub-Registrar and thus, ingredients of offences under Sections 420/ 466/ 467/ 471/ 120-B/ 34 IPC are clearly made out.
